          "number": 4,
          "letter": "D",
          "english": "Seven in 10 workers say they struggle to maintain work-life balance. As technology (and with it, work emails) seeps(渗入) into every aspect of our lives, work-life balance has become an almost meaningless term. Add a rapidly changing economy and an uncertain future to this 24/7 connectivity, and you've got a recipe for overwork, according to Phyllis Moen. \"There's rising work demand coupled with the insecurity of mergers, takeovers, downsizing and other factors,\" Moen said. \"Part of the work-life issue has to talk about uncertainty about the future.\"",
